WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.040
So, the program really helped
me see where my potential lies.

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:10.380
Definitely, my vision
is completely different.

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:12.800
I have grown as a person in that respect.

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:15.340
But what it brought me
was a change in mindset,

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:17.780
greater self-knowledge,

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:22.860
and clarity about the path I
want for my professional life.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:29.140
Initially, I had a very narrow
view of my role and my team.

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:33.140
It was definitely a micro-level view.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:36.060
And now, after this training, I
have the opportunity to understand

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:40.380
how strategic decisions are
made at the corporate level.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:44.700
Yes, my thinking process has
changed on strategic matters.

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:48.960
From the beginning, defining
what our North Star is,

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:50.560
our mission and vision,

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:55.560
also helped me redefine my
decision-making process.

00:00:56.740 --> 00:00:58.760
What this program helped me do was evaluate

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:01.140
my own journey and what is important to me,

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:04.120
and define my North Star
and my personal values.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:10.340
The program itself allowed me to get
to know myself on a personal level.

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:11.660
And that is very powerful.

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:13.720
From this moment on,

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:19.360
I will use what I have learned
to become a better person,

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:22.160
to be a better leader in what I do,

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:25.420
and through that leadership,
share it with others.

00:01:25.660 --> 00:01:27.800
But I really didn't understand science,

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:28.720
although I understood some of it.

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:32.620
Now, with the program, I have
a much stronger command of it.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:37.540
Definitely, these tools make
decision-making much more effective,

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:41.000
and much more aware of the risks.

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:43.860
Over these last few weeks,
working together as a group,

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:46.220
we worked with the Lencioni pyramid,

00:01:46.220 --> 00:01:51.900
whose foundation is very clear: trust.

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:54.480
And we built that trust within our group,

00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:56.500
which we can apply to our teams,

00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:57.720
to the way we work together,

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:01.740
personally and with our work
partners within the ME group.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:05.680
Interpretations that allow me to
make decisions based on facts.

00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:12.420
I think these are very important
tools: LTV, CAC, churn rate,

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:19.900
all tools we can use to quantify value creation,
value proposition, and value within organizations.

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:24.900
These different models really
apply to business today.

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:28.780
This is something I can apply
immediately to my existing structure.

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:32.060
This program was really
helpful in empowering me

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:36.980
and in building that collaboration
with colleagues from the subsidiaries,

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:42.600
showing that we have the ability and
opportunity to develop our own ideas

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:46.760
instead of waiting for company initiatives:
collaborate and push ideas through the organization.

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:52.580
So we can think more strategically instead of
focusing on the day-to-day operational view.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:55.760
Thank you.
